   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Return and Emigration Assistance from the Netherlands (REAN) 2022-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme contributes to the management of return migration in the Netherlands through the provision of Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration (AVRR) support to eligible migrants in the Netherlands. This will be done through the provision of AVRR information and counselling to 15,000 migrants; the assistance of 6,600 migrants with their voluntary return from the Netherlands to the country of origin, or with their resettlement to a third country where their admission is guaranteed; the provision of reintegration support to 2,125 departing migrants and to assist with implementation of reintegration assistance another 246 departing migrants on behalf of Dutch referring organisations; the support to 980 returnees in a situation of vulnerability including 900 migrants with health concerns, 40 unaccompanied migrant children and 40 victims of trafficking; the promotion of AVRR programmes and of AVRR support available. To succeed, IOM depends on cooperation with IOM missions worldwide and multiple partners in the Netherlands and in the countries of origin, and on cooperation with donors.</narrative>
  </description>
